I have finally finished re-implementation of encryption in Bones.
The following are the still existing problems.

- The des routines need to be compatible with MIT version.
They are not currently.  Soon I will have access to binary version of
MIT's routines (they are shipped with ultrix 4) and I will attempt
(by brute force if needed :-) to make all of my routines 100% compatible
with the ultrix version.  This new version will be released when in the
next few weeks (I hope :-).

- rlogin -x and rcp -x could have problems when working with MIT's version

- Since I am about to get snowed under with other work,
I am sending out my version of encrypting Bones without as much
testing as I would like.  All the programs work here on the vax
architecture but I have not been able to test them on 68000, sparc or MIPS
processors yet.  If there are any problems/fixes needed, please
send them to me.

eric (eay@surf.sics.bu.oz.au)
